== Overview ==
Freebuff is not a search engine and not a chat box that only writes text back. The work is a loop: '''request → context → decision → tool call → result → next step'''.

Four layers are easy to collapse into one word:
{| class="wikitable"
! Layer !! What it decides
|-
| Model || Generates the reply and chooses the next action
|-
| Agent || Gives the model a role, instructions, project context and tools
|-
| Tool || Performs one concrete action: read a file, search text, run a command
|-
| Runtime || Where that action happens — your machine or a cloud workspace
|}

Freebuff is made by the Codebuff team on top of [https://codebuff.com Codebuff], an open multi-agent framework, and is often described as the free alternative to Claude Code, Codex CLI, Cursor, Windsurf and Devin. The source is public ([https://github.com/CodebuffAI/freebuff CodebuffAI/freebuff], Apache-2.0), and Freebuff reads <code>AGENTS.md</code> and <code>CLAUDE.md</code> so project rules you already wrote still apply.

== Platforms ==
{| class="wikitable sortable"
! Version !! What it is
|-
| Desktop || macOS, Windows and Linux. Runs agents on a local folder; parallel agents each get their own workspace.
|-
| CLI || <code>npm install -g freebuff</code>, then <code>freebuff</code>. Node 16+ per docs, 18+ per the CLI page; works over SSH and in tmux.
|-
| Web || Browser version at [https://freebuff.com/app freebuff.com/app], aimed at building and shipping full-stack apps.
|-
| Cloud || Runs agents on any GitHub repository, with sandbox, preview, terminal and deploy.
|-
| Chat || Free AI chat for questions and research, no project needed.
|-
| Mobile || iOS and Android apps; follow and continue chats started on Desktop.
|-
| Website Builder || Prompt-to-app with managed hosting and a live URL.
|-
| Cowork || A separate surface for non-coding work with the same agent.
|}

== Capabilities ==
'''Understand a project'''
* Map files and explain how the pieces fit together
* Search for a symbol, string or path; read big files by line range

'''Change code'''
* Edit files with exact-match replacements, or rewrite a file whole
* Create new files, refactor a large file into smaller ones

'''Run and verify'''
* Terminal commands: install, build, test, lint, scripts — with real side effects
* Run your own post-change hooks when they are configured
* Live preview of a running site, plus a real browser for clicking, typing, screenshots, console and network errors

'''Ship'''
* Publish a site with database, file storage and sign-in
* Work on a connected GitHub repository and open a pull request when asked

'''Produce content'''
* Documents, slides, spreadsheets and diagrams
* Images and simple page designs

'''Find information'''
* Web search plus page reading; a separate research helper for multi-source questions

'''Use your other apps'''
* GitHub, Linear, Notion, Stripe, Vercel, Supabase, Sentry, PostHog, Resend, Google Drive/Docs/Sheets, Discord, Telegram
* MCP servers you add and approve

'''Work in parallel'''
* Up to 6 helpers per spawn request; up to 20 code subagents at once with Projects access

