Plan mode makes the writing tools refuse. Some helpers — full code subagents — are offered only with Projects access, not in Plan and not on sponsored runs.

== How to start ==
# Open [https://freebuff.com freebuff.com] and download Desktop, or open the web app.
# Or: <code>npm install -g freebuff</code>, then run <code>freebuff</code> inside a project folder.
# Open an existing project, or start an empty folder.
# Ask something small first: ''"Explain what this project does."''
# Then one step at a time, checking the diff as you go.

'''Brief it like a ticket:'''
* '''Outcome''' — what is true when the task is done.
* '''Boundary''' — what it may touch and what it must leave alone.
* '''Check''' — the command, test or URL that proves it.

== Cost ==
Freebuff is funded by '''text ads''', not a subscription; paid plans add more model time.

* Balances are shown in '''hours''' since 2026-10-15. '''1 hour = 5 Freebucks.''' Freebucks still appear as the credit unit.
* A model costs hours at the rate in the picker: one-hour model = one hour of balance, three-hour model = three, free experimental models = none.
* Supported regions get full access. Other regions and VPN/proxy users get '''limited access''': 5 hours a day, or 4 with a VPN or proxy, spent first on every model.
* Referrals and bounties earn extra hours, which go into a wallet and are used after the daily allowance.

